  "starterCode": "# Layer Normalization — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, gamma=None, beta=None, eps=1e-5):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Layer Normalization** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, gamma=None, beta=None, eps=1e-5):\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); mean=x.mean(axis=-1,keepdims=True); var=((x-mean)**2).mean(axis=-1,keepdims=True)\n    y=(x-mean)/np.sqrt(var+eps)\n    if gamma is not None: y=y*np.asarray(gamma,dtype=float)\n    if beta is not None: y=y+np.asarray(beta,dtype=float)\n    return y.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
